Z||000011||turbo86se||05-27-2001||02:04 PM||||Believe me, I know what you're feeling. It took my mechanic just over a year to complete my '88 coupe V6 installation. That was a long year. Now I've got it back, drove it to Carlisle last weekend (put 1400 miles on it in 4 days) with only one check engine light (02 sensor) and have driven it every day. T-Tops leak and all, I don't care, I'm so glad to have it back. Nobody really felt too bad for me b/c of my turbo-charged mint '86SE sleeping in my garage.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If you're ever in Myrtle, email me. We'll get together!<P>Bill, glad to hear you're getting your Fiero back. Give me a call!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=1676320&p=20236791"> ||||reg||10
Z||000012||isthiswhereiputausername?||05-27-2001||02:22 PM||||My baby was garaged for the past 3 years.. stored it in the winter and was in the process of moving in the spring and that and working extra hours never left me much time to do anything to it.<P>Now that we have a house in the country.. with a garage that has a pit.. I will make the time to get her going  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Took it out last weekend for the first drive in 3 years  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   worked great after I replaced the plugs in it and replaced the battery..  Now if only I can locate a auto shift cable  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> .... shiftings really stiff  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>It sure feels nice to be behind the wheel of her again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>||||reg||9
